--- Reconciliation against the coordinator's own 158-line measurement (and a second, independent one of my own) ---
Coordinator's command, re-run at the SAME 3 refs, unchanged: 158 lines match at EACH of records/product/evidence
(confirmed independently before writing any fix). My own schema-based count is 186 rows per ref -- HIGHER, by 28,
not lower. Explained, not hand-waved: the coordinator's own regex is LINE-anchored
(^\s*(-\s+)?tests:\s*(\[|$)), so it only ever sees a "tests:" key written in YAML BLOCK style (its own line). This
repository's own release/root-of-trust/4.1.6/decision-register/DECISION_REGISTER.yaml writes its
procedure_inputs: and excluded_inputs: rows in FLOW style on ONE line each, e.g.
  - {id: PI-01, input: "...", role: selector, decision: DR-38, ..., tests: ["FA7:...", RT-184]}
  - {exclusion: EX-01, input: "...", role: excluded, mechanism: "...", tests: ["PROF7:EX-01", RT-190]}
-- 23 procedure_inputs rows (id: PI-NN) and 24 excluded_inputs rows (identifier key "exclusion", NOT in
REGISTRY_ROW_ID_KEYS -- correctly falls back to its own key-path: excluded_inputs/0 .. excluded_inputs/23) are
BOTH genuinely real registry rows a PARSED-YAML walk finds correctly and a raw LINE regex structurally cannot
(independently confirmed: `git show <commit>:.../DECISION_REGISTER.yaml | grep -c ...` finds only the 45
block-style decisions: rows in that one file; this build's own per-path breakdown finds 92 distinct row
identifiers there -- 45 decisions + 23 procedure_inputs + 24 excluded_inputs). This ONE file alone accounts for
+47 rows over what line-counting would show; the remaining files' rows net back down by the SAME ~19 files
already identified (in the second reopening's own check6/second-check-cycle work) as containing a "tests:" key
that is a MAPPING (RPT-*.yaml's own tests:{status,reason}, PROJECT_POLICY.yaml's tests:{product_test_command,
baseline_record}, migrations/M-4.1.5-4.1.6.yaml's identical shape) or a list of DICTS, never strings
(release/capability-baseline/verify-1/synthesis/evidence/AC-10-gov-contract-matrix-with-my-runs.yaml's own
resolved.tests:[{test,file,line}] rows) -- all correctly EXCLUDED by the schema (a list of strings, never a
mapping or a list of dicts), matching a "tests:" LINE by the coordinator's own pattern but never a genuine
registry row. No unexplained gap either direction.

--- Second, independent measurement of the zero-count EXACT_TEST_REGISTRY_ROW (BR-DAG-AMEND-R1-8 item 4) ---
A DIRECT SQL query against the real, persisted code_symbol table (no derive.py/lineage_layer.py resolution code
involved at all): `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM code_symbol WHERE is_test=1 AND qualified_name LIKE '%::%'` -> 0, out of
928 real is_test=1 symbols in the whole indexed corpus. Structurally explained, not a bug: this repository's own
tree-sitter adapter (rust_treesitter.py's own _walk) gives a qualified_name a "::"-prefix ONLY for a function
defined inside an `impl` block (Type::method); EVERY real #[test] function in this corpus is a plain top-level or
mod-nested free function, which the SAME adapter gives a BARE qualified_name (no module prefix at all,
independently confirmed with a synthetic tree-sitter parse in this reopening's own working notes). It is
therefore structurally impossible for the exact-full-string-match bucket to fire on this corpus today; the
bare-name fallback (351 HEURISTIC_TEST_REGISTRY_SYMBOL rows, 303 of them resolved-by-bare-name-uniquely) is the
realistic, honest precision tier for this corpus's own shape, exactly as the reopening ruling's own wording
anticipated ("EXACT when unique; a distinct HEURISTIC label otherwise").

--- Cost measurement ---
lineage's OWN persisted footprint stays small: lineage_edge 3904 rows, lineage_unresolved 0 -- unchanged in kind
from prior rounds. Registry resolution's real cost is the PREREQUISITE "core"+"code" layer indexing this
capability now genuinely depends on (occurrence/code_symbol/code_call_site/code_literal, needed by ANY consumer
of code-layer data, not specific to this feature): ~18-19s per build in this measurement (a fresh, throwaway
store, never store-BR-AR-0010); "lineage" layer's own wall time grew from round 3's ~326s average to ~353s
average (the extra ~27s split between the wider registry walk and the code_symbol JOIN lookups, once per ref).
Not disproportionate: still well under the semantic/embedding layer's own ~885s single-layer figure measured
earlier this run.
